Yes, you can plot the sums and averages of each column using MATLAB's built-in `bar` function. Here's the code to plot both the sums and averages in separate figures:

```
% Plotting sums
figure
bar(sums)
title('Column Sums')
xlabel('Column Number')
ylabel('Sum')

% Plotting averages
figure
bar(avgs)
title('Column Averages')
xlabel('Column Number')
ylabel('Average')
```

This will create two separate figures, one showing the sums of each column and the other showing the averages of each column. <|endoftext|>
