Can you explain the difference between homologous and analogous structures in biology?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Homologous structures are structures that have a similar origin but may have different functions, such as the wings of a bird and the arms of a human. Analogous structures, on the other hand, have a different origin but may have a similar function, such as the wings of a bird and the wings of a butterfly. <|endoftext|>
