2. Test the function with a minimum profit margin of 0%, and ensure that the output does not change from the original profit calculation.
3. Test the function with a minimum profit margin greater than 100%, and ensure that an error is thrown since it is impossible to achieve such a profit margin.
4. Test the function with negative values for cost, selling price, or units sold, and ensure that an error is thrown since these inputs do not make sense in the context of calculating profit.

By testing the function with a variety of input values and edge cases, you can ensure that it is working properly and will produce accurate results for any input that you provide. <|endoftext|>
