<|user|>
I have collected data on people's daily routines and their health conditions over a year. The data is stored in a SQL database as shown below:
TABLE: daily_routine
---------------------------------------
| user_id | date | hours_slept |
---------------------------------------
| 1 | 2020-01-01 | 8 |
| 1 | 2020-01-02 | 7 |
| 1 | 2020-01-03 | 9 |
| 2 | 2020-01-01 | 7 |
| 2 | 2020-01-02 | 6 |
| 2 | 2020-01-03 | 8 |
| 3 | 2020-01-01 | 9 |
| 3 | 2020-01-02 | 8 |
| 3 | 2020-01-03 | 9 |
...
Based on this data, can you provide an example of a daily routine that can be considered a healthy lifestyle? Please provide a SQL query that filters the results for users who have slept for at least 7 hours per day, exercised for at least 30 minutes per day, and consumed less than 30 grams of sugar per day, sorted by the number of days they have followed this routine.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure, here is a SQL query that filters the results for users who have slept for at least 7 hours per day, exercised for at least 30 minutes per day, and consumed less than 30 grams of sugar per day, sorted by the number of days they have followed this routine:
```
SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) as days_followed
FROM daily_routine
WHERE hours_slept >= 7 AND exercise_minutes >= 30 AND sugar_grams < 30
GROUP BY user_id
ORDER BY days_followed DESC;
```
Assuming that you have columns for exercise_minutes and sugar_grams in your daily_routine table, this query will count the number of days that each user has followed the healthy routine and sort the results in descending order based on the number of days followed. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
That's helpful! How would you modify the query to include only the users who have followed this routine for at least 60% of the year?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
To modify the query to include only the users who have followed this routine for at least 60% of the year, you can add a HAVING clause that filters the results based on the percentage of days that they have followed the routine. Here's the modified SQL query:

```
SELECT user_id, COUNT(*) as days_followed, 
 COUNT(*) / (365*0.6) as percent_followed
FROM daily_routine
WHERE hours_slept >= 7 AND exercise_minutes >= 30 AND sugar_grams < 30
GROUP BY user_id
HAVING percent_followed >= 1
ORDER BY days_followed DESC;
```

This query calculates the percentage of days that each user has followed the routine by dividing the number of days followed by 60% of the total number of days in a year (365*0.6). The HAVING clause filters the results to only include users who have followed the routine for at least 60% of the year (percent_followed >= 1). The results are then sorted based on the number of days followed in descending order. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


