The Higgs boson particle is an elementary particle in the Standard Model of particle physics. Its discovery confirmed the existence of the Higgs field, which is responsible for giving mass to other elementary particles. The Higgs boson helps us better understand the fundamental forces and building blocks of the universe. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


