<|end|>
<|asst|>
In SQL, a LEFT JOIN returns all the rows from the left table and the matching rows from the right table. If there is no match in the right table, NULL values are returned. A RIGHT JOIN does the opposite; it returns all the rows from the right table and the matching rows from the left table. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
