<|asst|>
1. Trello – Trello is a productivity app that enables individuals and teams to organise, track and manage projects, tasks, and ideas in one place. It makes it easy to share work, assign tasks and deadlines, and monitor progress in real-time.

2. RescueTime – RescueTime is a productivity app that tracks how you spend time on your phone, laptop or tablet, so you can gain insights into your productivity levels, identify time-wasting activities, and optimise your schedule for better results.

3. Slack – Slack is a team communication app that helps individuals and teams to collaborate, share files, and communicate in real-time. It makes it easy to stay connected and informed, even when working remotely.

4. Evernote – Evernote is a productivity app that lets users take notes, make to-do lists, and set reminders all in one place. It enables users to organise their thoughts and ideas, and keep track of important tasks and deadlines.

5. Focus@Will – Focus@Will is a productivity app that provides a personalised music playlist to help users stay focused, motivated and productive at work. It uses neuroscience-based music and soundscapes to improve concentration, creativity, and productivity levels. <|endoftext|>
