What code can I write to determine the highest elevation point in the Rocky Mountains range from this data?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
You can use a loop to iterate through the mountainRanges array and find the index of the "Rocky Mountains" range. Once you have the index, you can use it to access the corresponding elevation in the elevations array. Here's the C# code to accomplish this:
```
string[] mountainRanges = { "Rocky Mountains", "Appalachian Mountains", "Sierra Nevada Mountains" };
int[] elevations = { 14264, 6684, 14494 };
int highestElevation = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < mountainRanges.Length; i++)
{
 if (mountainRanges[i] == "Rocky Mountains")
 {
 highestElevation = elevations[i];
 break;
 }
}
