To calculate the average elevation of all the mountain ranges in the C# array, you need to first compute the sum of all elevations and then divide it by the total number of mountain ranges. Here's the C# code to accomplish this:
```
string[] mountainRanges = { "Rocky Mountains", "Appalachian Mountains", "Sierra Nevada Mountains" };
int[] elevations = { 14264, 6684, 14494 };
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < elevations.Length; i++)
{
 sum += elevations[i];
}
double averageElevation = (double)sum / elevations.Length;
