fmod(10.5, 3.2) + trunc(4.7) * round(2.3)=
<|end|>
<|asst|>
fmod(10.5, 3.2) will give the remainder when 10.5 is divided by 3.2, which is approximately 1.7. 
trunc(4.7) will give the integer part of 4.7, which is 4. 
round(2.3) will give the nearest integer to 2.3, which is 2. 
So, the expression becomes: 
1.7 + 4 * 2 
= 1.7 + 8 
= 9.7 
Therefore, fmod(10.5, 3.2) + trunc(4.7) * round(2.3) is approximately equal to 9.7. <|endoftext|>
