JavaScript Code for Adding an Accessory:
```
function addAccessory() {
 var accessorySelect = document.getElementById("accessorySelect");
 var selectedAccessory = accessorySelect.options[accessorySelect.selectedIndex].value;
 if (selectedAccessory != "") {
 var accessoryImg = document.createElement("img");
 accessoryImg.src = selectedAccessory;
 accessoryImg.alt = "Fashion Accessory";
 accessoryImg.width = "300";
 accessoryImg.height = "400";
 document.querySelector(".outfit").appendChild(accessoryImg);
 }
}
```
Explanation of the JavaScript Code:
1. The `addAccessory()` function is called when the user clicks the "Add" button.
2. The function first retrieves the `accessorySelect` element and the value of the selected option.
3. If an accessory is selected (i.e., the value is not empty), the function creates a new `img` element with the source and dimensions of the selected accessory.
4. The `img` element is then appended to the `.outfit` div using the `appendChild()` method.
The user can now select a fashion accessory from the dropdown menu and click the "Add" button to add it to the outfit showcase. The JavaScript code dynamically adds the accessory image to the HTML page. <|endoftext|>
