<|user|>
What SQL database query can I use to generate a unique four-letter word?
Here is the code you can use:
CREATE TABLE words (
 id INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
 word VARCHAR(4) UNIQUE
);
INSERT INTO words (word)
SELECT CONCAT(
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65)
)
FROM (
 SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 2 UNION SELECT 3 UNION SELECT 4 UNION SELECT 5
) t1
CROSS JOIN (
 SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 2 UNION SELECT 3 UNION SELECT 4 UNION SELECT 5
) t2;
SELECT word FROM words WHERE id = LAST_INSERT_ID();
<|end|>
<|asst|>
This SQL database query creates a table called "words" with an auto-incrementing ID and a unique four-letter word column. It then inserts a randomly generated four-letter word into the table and selects the word with the last inserted ID. Here is the query:
```
CREATE TABLE words (
 id INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
 word VARCHAR(4) UNIQUE
);
INSERT INTO words (word)
SELECT CONCAT(
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65),
 CHAR(FLOOR(RAND() * 26) + 65)
)
FROM (
 SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 2 UNION SELECT 3 UNION SELECT 4 UNION SELECT 5
) t1
CROSS JOIN (
 SELECT 1 UNION SELECT 2 UNION SELECT 3 UNION SELECT 4 UNION SELECT 5
) t2;
SELECT word FROM words WHERE id = LAST_INSERT_ID();
``` <|endoftext|>
