How does the concept of entropy relate to the second law of thermodynamics?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The concept of entropy is closely related to the second law of thermodynamics, which states that the total entropy of a closed system will always increase over time. Entropy is a measure of the disorder or randomness of a system, and the second law of thermodynamics predicts that systems will tend towards increasing levels of disorder over time. In other words, the second law of thermodynamics predicts that natural processes will always result in an increase in entropy. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
