The result of this calculation is stored in the "result" variable. The bitwise AND operator (&) is used to check if the least significant bit of "num1" is 1. If it is, "num2" is added to "result". The right shift operator (>>) is used to shift "num1" to the right by one bit, while the left shift operator (<<) is used to shift "num2" to the left by one bit. <|endoftext|>
