1. Grilled Salmon with Green Beans and Rice Pilaf
- Preheat the grill to medium-high heat.
- Season the salmon fillet with salt and pepper, and grill for 4-5 minutes on each side, until cooked through.
- Steam the green beans for 5-7 minutes, until tender.
- In a saucepan, sauté the onion and garlic in butter until softened.
- Add the rice and stir to coat in the butter mixture.
- Pour in the chicken broth and bring to a boil.
- Reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 18-20 minutes, until the rice is cooked.
- Serve the grilled salmon with the steamed green beans and rice pilaf.

2. Romaine Salad with Goat Cheese and Roasted Almonds
- Wash and chop the romaine lettuce and place in a salad bowl.
- Crumble the goat cheese over the top of the lettuce.
- Toast the almonds in a dry skillet over medium heat for a few minutes, until fragrant.
- Sprinkle the almonds over the salad.
- Drizzle the salad with your favorite dressing, such as balsamic vinaigrette or honey mustard.

These recipes are easy to follow and use all of the ingredients from the grocery list. Enjoy! <|endoftext|>
