pow(2, 4) + pow(3, 3) - pow(4, 2) * pow(5, 1)=
<|end|>
<|asst|>
The expression pow(2, 4) means 2 raised to the power of 4, which is 16. Similarly, pow(3, 3) means 3 raised to the power of 3, which is 27. And pow(4, 2) * pow(5, 1) means 4 raised to the power of 2 multiplied by 5 raised to the power of 1, which is 80. 
So, the expression pow(2, 4) + pow(3, 3) - pow(4, 2) * pow(5, 1) can be simplified as:
16 + 27 - 80 = -37
Therefore, the answer is -37. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
