<|asst|>
Certainly! In Greek mythology, Prometheus was a Titan who stole fire from the gods and gave it to humanity. He was punished for his actions, but his gift to humans allowed them to progress and advance in ways that they never could have without fire. Similarly, in "Frankenstein," Victor Frankenstein creates life from dead body parts using the power of electricity, just as Prometheus brought the gift of fire to humanity. The subtitle "The Modern Prometheus" therefore draws a parallel between these two figures and suggests that Victor's creation is a symbol of human progress and innovation, but also carries with it the potential for great danger and consequences. <|endoftext|>
