Over time, chaturanga spread throughout Asia and into the Middle East, where it evolved into shatranj, a similar game with slightly different pieces and rules. Shatranj became incredibly popular in the Islamic world and eventually spread to Europe through trade routes and conquests.

In the late Middle Ages, the modern version of chess began to take shape in Europe, with the addition of the queen and the bishop pieces and changes to the way the pieces move. Since then, chess has continued to evolve and develop as people around the world play and study the game. <|endoftext|>
