<|asst|>
LaTeX is a document preparation system that uses markup language to format text. It allows users to focus on the content of their document rather than worrying about the appearance. The user inputs plain text with some additional markup, such as commands to format headings, lists, and tables, and then LaTeX processes this input to produce a formatted document. One of the key advantages of using LaTeX is that it provides consistent formatting across all documents, making it easier to create professional-looking documents with minimal effort. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
I'm curious about the history of LaTeX. When was it first created, and by whom?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
LaTeX was created in the 1980s by Leslie Lamport, a computer scientist at Digital Equipment Corporation (DEC). Lamport originally created LaTeX as an extension of Donald Knuth's TeX typesetting system, which was designed for producing high-quality technical documents. LaTeX quickly became popular among academics and researchers due to its ability to easily produce complex mathematical equations and other technical content. Today, LaTeX is used by millions of people around the world for a wide range of document types, from academic papers and books to business reports and presentations. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
