Chelonians such as the turtle with their scaly, bony, and protective shell covering their body.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Chelonians, including turtles, are reptiles. They are characterized by their scaly skin, cold-blooded metabolism, and the presence of a protective bony shell covering their body. Mammals, on the other hand, are characterized by their warm-blooded metabolism, hair or fur, and mammary glands that produce milk for their young. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
