Yes, that was helpful. Could you also provide an example of a commonly used algorithm for each type of learning?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Of course! Some common supervised learning algorithms include linear regression, logistic regression, decision trees, random forests, and neural networks. These algorithms are often used for tasks like classification, regression, and prediction.

For unsupervised learning, some popular algorithms include k-means clustering, hierarchical clustering, principal component analysis (PCA), and t-SNE. These algorithms are often used for tasks like feature extraction, dimensionality reduction, and anomaly detection.

