<|end|>
<|asst|>
Dark matter is a hypothetical form of matter that has not been directly observed, but is thought to make up about 85% of the matter in the universe. Its existence is inferred from its gravitational effects on visible matter, and its study is important in understanding the large-scale structure of the universe and the formation of galaxies. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>


