Could you explain the concept of machine learning in simple terms?
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Sure! Machine learning is a type of artificial intelligence (AI) that enables computers to learn and improve from experience without being explicitly programmed. In other words, instead of telling a computer exactly what to do, we give it a set of examples or data and have it learn patterns and correlations on its own. These patterns can then be used to make predictions or decisions about new data. Think of it like this - imagine you wanted to teach a child how to recognize different animals. You could show them pictures of animals and tell them what each one is called until they can recognize each one on their own. Machine learning works in a similar way, except the "child" is a computer program and the "pictures" are datasets. <|endoftext|>
