Imagine you are organizing an event and want to create an immersive experience for attendees by integrating virtual reality technology into your program. However, you want to make sure that the VR aspect of the program is only activated when the attendee meets certain conditions. 
To do this, you decide to create a C++ program that includes a calculation puzzle. The program will only activate the VR technology when the attendee solves the puzzle correctly. 
Here's the puzzle: 
You have a box containing 10 white balls and 10 black balls. You randomly draw 3 balls from the box without replacement. What is the probability that you draw 2 white balls and 1 black ball? 
Once the attendee solves the puzzle correctly, the VR technology will be activated, providing an immersive experience.
<|end|>
<|asst|>
Here's a C++ program that solves the puzzle and activates the VR technology:
```
#include 
using namespace std;
int main() {
 int whiteBalls = 10;
 int blackBalls = 10;
 int totalBalls = whiteBalls + blackBalls;
 int numDraws = 3;
 int numWhite = 2;
 int numBlack = 1;
 double probability = 1.0;
 for (int i = 0; i < numWhite; i++) {
 probability *= (double)(whiteBalls - i) / (totalBalls - i);
 }
 for (int i = 0; i < numBlack; i++) {
 probability *= (double)(blackBalls - i) / (totalBalls - numWhite - i);
 }
 probability *= factorial(numDraws) / (factorial(numWhite) * factorial(numBlack) * factorial(numDraws - numWhite - numBlack));
 if (probability == 0.1176) {
 activateVR();
 }
 return 0;
}
int factorial(int n) {
 int result = 1;
 for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
 result *= i;
 }
 return result;
}
void activateVR() {
 // Code to activate VR technology goes here
}
```
The program first sets up the variables for the number of white balls, black balls, total balls, and number of draws. It then sets the expected number of white and black balls drawn and calculates the probability using the formula for the hypergeometric distribution. If the probability matches the expected value of 0.1176, the `activateVR()` function is called to activate the VR technology. <|endoftext|>
<|end|>
<|user|>
